            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "What do you think of adding this at the end?\n\n```\n`libmctp` does _not_ provide abstractions for Linux's MCTP sockets. Examples of how to use MCTP\nsockets can be found in the [introduction to MCTP on Linux][mctp-on-linux-introduction].\n\n[mctp-on-linux-introduction]: https://codeconstruct.com.au/docs/mctp-on-linux-introduction/\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Or maybe just adding:\n\n```\nYou do not need to use `libmctp` to make use of that sockets-based interface.\n```\n\nI didn't want to be pushing the cc docs too much, nor put too much description of the non-libmctp approach, hence keeping it fairly short and not including the link here.\n\nHowever, if you think that adds to the description, I can certainly be persuaded!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, I'm fine with your suggestion. Just from experience some seem to have the impression they need to use a library to abstract over kernel interfaces (true in other circumstances; libgpiod, liburing etc), so I think it's worth emphasising it's not necessary here. The link to the doc wasn't so much promotional as directly demonstrating that. Maybe https://docs.kernel.org/networking/mctp.html is better, but if you don't think we need it then I'm happy to not have it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, makes sense; agree on the library abstraction point. I'll rework and push a new change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
